  "title": "Linux-7.1.8 API Headers",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "section",
      "title": "",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Linux API Headers (in linux-7.1.8.tar.xz) expose the kernel's API for use by Glibc."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "segmented_list",
          "titles": [
            "Approximate build time",
            "Required disk space"
          ],
          "values": [
            "less than 0.1 SBU",
            "1.8 GB"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "role": "package"
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "title": "Installation of Linux API Headers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Linux kernel needs to expose an Application Programming Interface (API) for the system's C library (Glibc in LFS) to use. This is done by way of sanitizing various C header files that are shipped in the Linux kernel source tarball."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Make sure there are no stale files embedded in the package:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bootstrap_command",
          "index": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Now extract the user-visible kernel headers from the source. The recommended make target"
            },
            {
              "type": "quote",
              "text": "headers_install"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "cannot be used, because it requires"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "rsync"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", which may not be available. The headers are first placed in"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "text": "./usr"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", then copied to the needed location."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bootstrap_command",
              "index": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bootstrap_command",
              "index": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "role": "installation"
    },
